================================================================================
INSTALLATION & ENVIRONMENT SETUP GUIDE
CUDA at Scale for the Enterprise - Final Project
================================================================================

This document provides step-by-step instructions for compiling and executing
the CUDA & NPP Scalable Image Processing Enterprise Pipeline across different
platforms and environments.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Coursera Laboratory Environment / Linux with NVIDIA GPU
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Coursera Lab environment provides pre-configured NVIDIA GPUs (Turing/Ampere)
and CUDA Toolkit installations under /usr/local/cuda.

Steps:
1. Open a terminal session in the lab environment.
2. Clone or extract the project repository:
     cd ~
     git clone <YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL> cuda_npp_project
     cd cuda_npp_project

3. Verify CUDA environment:
     nvcc --version
     nvidia-smi

4. Prepare the dataset (downloads/generates USC-SIPI images):
     python3 scripts/prepare_dataset.py --output_dir data/input --num_small 100

5. Build the GPU-accelerated binary using Make:
     make all -j4

6. Execute the automated benchmark and verification script:
     ./run.sh

   Or run individual commands:
     ./bin/cuda_image_proc --input_dir data/input --output_dir output/large --filter all --benchmark

7. Generated artifacts:
   Execution logs and packaged submission archives will be created in:
     - artifacts/execution_log.txt
     - artifacts/benchmark_report.md
     - artifacts/execution_artifacts.tar.gz

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. macOS / Development Machines without NVIDIA GPU
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

On machines without an NVIDIA GPU or NVCC (such as Apple Silicon or CPU-only
workstations), the codebase includes a full algorithmic simulation verification
backend that validates pipeline mechanics, Netpbm I/O, argument parsing,
and filtering accuracy.

Steps:
1. Open Terminal on macOS:
     cd /path/to/cuda_npp_project

2. Generate the USC-SIPI dataset:
     python3 scripts/prepare_dataset.py --output_dir data/input --num_small 100

3. Compile using Clang or GCC:
     make sim HOST_CXX=clang++ -j4
     # or: make sim HOST_CXX=g++ -j4

4. Run the complete pipeline and verification suite:
     ./run.sh

5. Inspect generated output images in:
     output/large/
     output/batch_small/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Verifying Installation & Outputs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To verify that the installation succeeded:
1. Ensure the binary exists:
     ls -l bin/cuda_image_proc   (on GPU systems)
     ls -l bin/sim_image_proc    (on simulation hosts)

2. Check that processed PGM images are populated in output/:
     ls -lh output/large/ | head -n 15

3. Verify packaged artifact:
     tar -tzvf artifacts/execution_artifacts.tar.gz | head -n 20
================================================================================
